#
# hosts - where cigbuild may download sources, signatures and signed tags from.
# One host per line, then what it is. Anything else is refused.
#
# Allowed: the big open source forges, and a project's OWN official release site. Never
# SourceForge, generic download sites or third-party mirrors. A host is never what makes a
# file authentic (that is the signature or the pinned checksum); this list decides where
# cig is willing to fetch from at all. Add an official site only with its project named.
#
# Forges redirect downloads to their own CDNs (codeload.github.com, ...): the check applies
# to the URL in the recipe.

# forges
github.com                  forge
gitlab.com                  forge
codeberg.org                forge
git.sr.ht                   forge
gitlab.freedesktop.org      forge (freedesktop.org)
gitlab.alpinelinux.org      forge (Alpine Linux: aports files used by linux, elfutils)

